{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$f$", "MATH_0003": "$\\Delta_{X/S}$", "MATH_0004": "$f$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Delta_{X/S}$", "MATH_0006": "$Y$", "MATH_0007": "$Y \\to \\Spec(\\mathbf{Z})$", "MATH_0008": "$Y$", "MATH_0009": "$Y \\to \\Spec(\\mathbf{Z})$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\begin{enumerate}", "STRUCT_0002": "\\item", "STRUCT_0003": "\\item", "STRUCT_0004": "\\item", "STRUCT_0005": "\\item", "STRUCT_0006": "\\end{enumerate}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0003": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0004": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0003": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0004": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4c0f280ef64fc4f381cdc6ce4906bbacea3f499ee11c512ffacebcd7caf07dd6", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:bfad589a82d905040b35b038bf21de2cb170c514d82b083f56777f7ca26a5c69", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\n<STRUCT_0001>\n<STRUCT_0002> We say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>separated<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if the diagonal morphism <MATH_0003>\nis a closed immersion.\n<STRUCT_0003> We say <MATH_0004> is <TEXTITOPEN_0002>quasi-separated<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> if the diagonal morphism\n<MATH_0005> is a quasi-compact morphism.\n<STRUCT_0004> We say a scheme <MATH_0006> is <TEXTITOPEN_0003>separated<TEXTITCLOSE_0003> if the morphism\n<MATH_0007> is separated.\n<STRUCT_0005> We say a scheme <MATH_0008> is <TEXTITOPEN_0004>quasi-separated<TEXTITCLOSE_0004> if the morphism\n<MATH_0009> is quasi-separated.\n<STRUCT_0006>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:df6be6ec24f53142bbb2fa9cf73ba750f8218699f27fe0ab2c6a0c9a62ade80d", "unit_id": "tag:01KK:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\Delta_{X/S}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\Delta_{X/S}(X) \\subset X \\times_S X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-diagonal-immersion}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-immersion-when-closed}", "REF_0003": "\\ref{lemma-closed-immersion-quasi-compact}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:92d36a62c26fa5f88eb19216c7b68538c78ca358184e2055e02e103390562317", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:72e0c2462cef535e7cc0cf308ab6713ad52f9782dfb67c5eaa26c316f1b00b5a", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nBy Lemmas <REF_0001> and <REF_0002>\nwe see that <MATH_0001> is a closed immersion if an only if\n<MATH_0002> is a closed subset. Moreover,\nby Lemma <REF_0003> we see that a\nseparated morphism is quasi-separated. The reason for introducing\nquasi-separated morphisms is that nonseparated morphisms come up naturally\nin studying algebraic varieties (especially when doing moduli,\nalgebraic stacks, etc). But most often they are still quasi-separated.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:68d2610c9633f056044b0a895d88f1f1a51c5a829fd7d7b88fe5e080bbf6b62c", "unit_id": "tag:01KH:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "example", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X = X_1 \\cup X_2 \\to S = \\Spec(k)$", "MATH_0002": "$X_1 = X_2 = \\Spec(k[t_1, t_2, t_3, \\ldots])$", "MATH_0003": "$\\{0\\} = \\{(t_1, t_2, t_3, \\ldots)\\}$", "MATH_0004": "$X_1 \\times_S X_2$", "MATH_0005": "$\\Delta_{X/S}$", "MATH_0006": "$\\Spec(k[t_1, t_2, t_3, \\ldots]) \\setminus \\{0\\}$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{example-affine-space-zero-doubled}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{example}\n\\label{example-not-quasi-separated}\n", "suffix": "\\end{example}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:53509ccb46f348e2fca0f1e1839dbb7eb8a0210341902731e0924db374523060", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8d8fcc89119aec54c271a7231fda75517a630cbc4ca950fd2b52457c2a7bda6e", "source_text": "Here is an example of a non-quasi-separated morphism.\nSuppose <MATH_0001> with\n<MATH_0002>\nglued along the complement of <MATH_0003>\n(glued as in Example <REF_0001>).\nIn this case the inverse image of the affine scheme\n<MATH_0004> under <MATH_0005> is the scheme\n<MATH_0006>\nwhich is not quasi-compact.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5c05672c13018d05c74c509e6dab5799d6a886912256247b2084c7225a99c860", "unit_id": "tag:01KL:statement"}
{"chapter": "schemes", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "01KH", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$Y$", "MATH_0003": "$S$", "MATH_0004": "$a, b : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0005": "$S$", "MATH_0006": "$Z \\subset X$", "MATH_0007": "$a|_Z = b|_Z$", "MATH_0008": "$Z$", "MATH_0009": "$(a, b)$", "MATH_0010": "$Y$", "MATH_0011": "$S$", "MATH_0012": "$Z$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-where-are-they-equal}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bbd0a569724793c1e44c79df76acb9f6b019a283607069de9292ce5976ed8d8b", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:763b7c19066892df1cf02bafb4b33e1b3c5884b8847448a01066acb8076ca668", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001>, <MATH_0002> be schemes over <MATH_0003>.\nLet <MATH_0004> be morphisms of schemes over <MATH_0005>.\nThere exists a largest locally closed subscheme\n<MATH_0006> such that <MATH_0007>. In fact <MATH_0008> is\nthe equalizer of <MATH_0009>. Moreover, if <MATH_0010> is separated\nover <MATH_0011>, then <MATH_0012> is a closed subscheme.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0541397c17947873cb64606dccc75f2a475548ee5caa7628e979adc223ad9ace", "unit_id": "tag:01KM:statement"}
